# LANTERN law 1: matter is honest (docs/LOOK.md). The SAME machine, the same
# kind, the same pose, in four landscapes, and the land it is standing in is
# what has happened to it -- rust creeping up its underside in the bog, soot in
# its lee in the Burning, a pale bloom out of its seams on the bone, frost on
# what faces the sky in the snow. Nobody authored four harvesters.
#
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/matter.tour --seed=7 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0
#
# Eleven in the morning and a clear sky on purpose: the wear has to read in
# plain daylight, not be rescued by a mood. The frames are meant to be laid
# side by side -- that is the whole proof, and it is why they are all one zoom
# and one hour.
weather clear:0
hour 11
zoom 8

place moss
wait 0.8
spawn harvester
wait 0.5
shot 01-rusting-in-the-bog with mob:harvester,land:moss

place burning
wait 0.8
spawn harvester
wait 0.5
shot 02-sooted-in-the-burning with mob:harvester,land:burning

place bonelands
wait 0.8
spawn harvester
wait 0.5
shot 03-bloomed-on-the-bone with mob:harvester,land:bonelands

place snowfield
wait 0.8
spawn harvester
wait 0.5
shot 04-frosted-on-the-snow with mob:harvester,land:snowfield

# And the land itself takes a little of it, so a house and a fence in the bog
# belong to the bog the same way the machine does.
place moss
wait 0.8
zoom 14
shot 05-the-bog-and-what-stands-in-it with land:moss
place burning
wait 0.8
shot 06-the-burning-and-what-stands-in-it with land:burning
